# T2 chain fixtures and the tool that writes them are BYTE-compared:
# docs/chain-fixtures.md F1 fixes the encoding at "UTF-8, LF", DoD 3/4 compare whole
# files byte-for-byte, and the vendoring rule (chain_fixture.py is copied into every
# engine repo and checked by sha256) needs the script's bytes to be identical too.
#
# This repository has core.autocrlf enabled and, until this file, no attributes at
# all - so a Windows checkout rewrote every text file to CRLF. That is invisible for
# C# sources and fatal for a byte comparison: the committed fixture would arrive with
# CRLF line endings while chain_fixture.py always writes LF, and every byte-identity
# assertion would fail on the Windows leg only.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
tests/chain-fixtures/** text eol=lf
